# Keep the published set to real site content.
#
# surge's built-in ignore (surge-ignore) already drops `.git`, every dotfile or
# dot-directory (which covers `.env`, `.env.*`, `.github`, `.gitignore`,
# `.surgeignore` and `.DS_Store`) and `node_modules`. The entries below are the
# non-dotfile leftovers we never want to serve.
#
# `CNAME` is deliberately excluded: surge reads it as the project's *local*
# domain identity (and writes one on success), but this workflow always passes
# the domain explicitly, so a source CNAME would only be uploaded and served as
# a stray file.
.github
.env
.env.*
CNAME
*.md
*.sh
README.md
temp-for-publish

# Explicit belt-and-braces (already covered by the built-in `.*` rule).
.git
.gitignore
.surgeignore
.DS_Store
node_modules
